                "Land was classified into four categories: Polaj (cultivated annually), Parauti (fallow 1–2 yrs), Chachar (fallow 3–4 yrs), and Banjar (uncultivated 5+ yrs).",
                "Alternative revenue methods included Ghalla-Bakhshi (Batai), Kankut (crop estimation), and Nasaq (summary settlement)."
